{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f4cbfc58a683894a66b028420969bb75a35fe4acda1bd3dce0024062c11b2041", "sample_idx": 18, "model_name": "mistralai/mixtral-8x7b-instruct-v0.1", "content": " \"The opening section of a news article from the Guardian is presented below. To view the print version, please follow the provided link. The standard regulations of Sudoku apply, with the exception that the figures in the cells enclosed by gray lines should equal the numbers in the corner. It is important to note that no number can appear more than once within each form created by the gray lines. To see the finished puzzle, readers are encouraged to purchase the following week's Observer Digital Edition.\"\n\nAddition to the classic Sudoku game is a new twist. In this version, there are certain areas of the puzzle that are enclosed by gray lines. The numbers present in these sections must equal the target number located in the corner of the same shape. It is crucial to remember that no number can be repeated within each distinct shape created by the gray lines.\n\nTo clarify, each gray-lined shape in the puzzle has a specific target number that must be reached by adding up the numbers in the cells within that shape. This is an extra challenge to the traditional Sudoku game, where the objective is simply to fill in the grid with numbers from 1 to 9, making sure that every row, column, and 3x3 box contains each number exactly once.\n\nInterestingly, this new version of Sudoku adds a layer of complexity to the game. Players must not only ensure that the numbers in the rows, columns, and boxes are unique but also that the numbers in each gray-lined shape add up to the target number. This makes the game more challenging and engaging for Sudoku enthusiasts looking for an extra challenge.\n\nTo see the completed puzzle, readers are advised to purchase the Observer Digital Edition of the following week. The solution to the puzzle will be revealed, and players can check their answers to see if they have successfully met the challenge. This is a great way to keep players engaged and motivated to improve their Sudoku skills.\n\nIn conclusion, the Guardian has introduced an exciting new twist to the classic Sudoku game. By adding gray-lined shapes that must add up to a target number, the game becomes more challenging and engaging for players. To see the finished puzzle and check their answers, readers can purchase the Observer Digital Edition of the following week.", "logprobs": [{"token": "\"", "logprob": -0.0005287918029353023}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -0.8779466152191162}, {"token": "opening", "logprob": -1.590667724609375}, {"token": "section", "logprob": -2.4094197750091553}, {"token": "of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "a", "logprob": -1.3174364566802979}, {"token": "news", "logprob": -0.006746253930032253}, {"token": "article", "logprob": -0.00016437610611319542}, {"token": "from", "logprob": -0.8937733769416809}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -0.006716177798807621}, {"token": "Guard", "logprob": -8.535020606359467e-05}, {"token": "ian", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "is", "logprob": -0.202621728181839}, {"token": "presented", "logprob": -0.0037306013982743025}, {"token": "below", "logprob": -0.002856937935575843}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.0024946779012680054}, {"token": "To", "logprob": -1.0713517665863037}, {"token": "view", "logprob": -0.00044526674901135266}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -3.540453326422721e-05}, {"token": "print", "logprob": -0.046312492340803146}, {"token": "version", "logprob": -0.0007295330869965255}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0007099968497641385}, {"token": "please", "logprob": -1.4497957229614258}, {"token": "follow", "logprob": -0.005527806468307972}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -0.003600069787353277}, {"token": "provided", "logprob": -0.0030277385376393795}, {"token": "link", "logprob": -5.483612312673358e-06}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -3.4570634852570947e-06}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -0.